subsection.p:
There is also a row-by-column formula. If A=(a_{ij}) is m\times n, and B=(b_{ij}) is p\times m, then BA is p\times n, and its (i,j)-entry is
\boxed{ (BA)_{ij} = b_{i1}a_{1j}+b_{i2}a_{2j}+\cdots+b_{im}a_{mj}. }
This formula is useful for calculation, but the meaning is the same: first apply A, then apply B.

