subsection.p:
\text{Different path limits disprove a limit.}
But
\text{matching path limits along many chosen paths do not prove a limit.}

Define

  S(x,y)=
  \begin{cases}
  \dfrac{xy}{x^2+y^2}, & (x,y)\ne(0,0),\\[2mm]
  0, & (x,y)=(0,0).
  \end{cases}

Define
M(x,y)= \begin{cases} 1, & 0\lt y\lt x^4,\\ 0, & \text{otherwise}. \end{cases}
Near the origin, the region 0\lt y\lt x^4 is a very thin strip above the x-axis.

