subsection.p:
The same triangular flower bed can also be described by horizontal slices. Since y=\frac{x}{2} is the same as x=2y, the triangle can be written as D= \left\{ (x,y): 0\le y\le2,\ 2y\le x\le4 \right\}. Thus
V \amp= \int_0^2\int_{2y}^4 (6-y)\,dx\,dy \amp= \int_0^2 (6-y)(4-2y)\,dy \amp= \int_0^2 (24-16y+2y^2)\,dy \amp= \left[ 24y-8y^2+\frac23y^3 \right]_0^2 \amp= 48-32+\frac{16}{3} \amp= \frac{64}{3}.
This matches the answer from vertical slices: \boxed{\frac{64}{3}.}

