subsection.p:
From x=r\cos\theta, \qquad y=r\sin\theta, regard x(r,\theta) and y(r,\theta) as scalar functions on the parameter plane. Their differentials there are d(x(r,\theta))=\cos\theta\,dr-r\sin\theta\,d\theta, and d(y(r,\theta))=\sin\theta\,dr+r\cos\theta\,d\theta. Now wedge:
d(x(r,\theta))\wedge d(y(r,\theta)) \amp= (\cos\theta\,dr-r\sin\theta\,d\theta) \wedge (\sin\theta\,dr+r\cos\theta\,d\theta) \amp= r\cos^2\theta\,dr\wedge d\theta + r\sin^2\theta\,dr\wedge d\theta \amp= r(\cos^2\theta+\sin^2\theta)\,dr\wedge d\theta \amp= r\,dr\wedge d\theta.
So the standard area form becomes \boxed{ d(x(r,\theta))\wedge d(y(r,\theta))=r\,dr\wedge d\theta. } This expresses target signed area in parameter coordinates; the two forms are not being identified on different planes. will name this operation pullback. For ordinary positive area, \boxed{ dA=r\,dr\,d\theta. }

